  Fail-degraded availability under QBER injection: 0.9703
  Fail-degraded availability under classical denial:  0.3127   (delta -0.6576)
  A post-quantum fallback needs the classical channel. Denying that
  channel removes the fallback, so fail-degraded is NOT immune --
  it is immune only to attacks on the QUANTUM channel.

